Current:
```java
    public synchronized void connectRelay(HostRelayConnector connector) {
        if (relayConnector != null) throw new IllegalStateException("Relay connector is already configured");
        relayConnector = java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(connector, "connector");
        relayConnector.start();
    }
```
New:
```java
    /**
     * Applies a Relay tunnel, replacing any tunnel already running. Relay configuration is reconfigurable, so a
     * repeated call is the normal path: the previous tunnel is closed before the new one starts and no
     * "already configured" terminal state exists.
     */
    public synchronized void connectRelay(HostRelayConnector connector) {
        HostRelayConnector next = java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(connector, "connector");
        HostRelayConnector previous = relayConnector;
        relayConnector = next;
        if (previous != null) previous.close();
        next.start();
    }

    /** Applies persisted Relay settings to this running Host. */
    public void applyRelay(RelaySettings settings) {
        connectRelay(relayEnrollment.tunnelFactory().create(settings,
                new RelayTunnelContext(hcp, devices, relayChallenges, sessions)));
    }
```
Hmm — `applyRelay` is public because ji-cli calls it at startup for persisted settings. OK.

And `hostRelay(exchange)`:
```java
    private void hostRelay(HttpExchange exchange) throws IOException {
        requireAuthenticated(exchange);
        RelayEnrollmentService service = relayService;
        if (service == null) throw notFound(exchange.getRequestURI().getPath());
        if ("GET".equals(exchange.getRequestMethod())) {
            json(exchange, 200, service.status(relayConnected()));
            return;
        }
        requireMethod(exchange, "POST");
        Map<String, Object> body = readMap(exchange);
        json(exchange, 200, service.configure(new RelayEnrollmentService.Command(
                text(body, "managementUrl"), text(body, "authorization"), optionalText(body, "bearer"),
                optionalText(body, "tenantId"), integer(body.get("expectedRevision"))), relayConnected()));
    }
```
Need helpers: `optionalText`. `text(...)` in LocalHostServer is `requiredText(Map, name)` — let me check the signature: `private static String requiredText(Map<String, Object> values, String name)`. Yes. And `number(Object)` exists returning long.

`relayConnected()`: `HostRelayConnector connector = relayConnector; return connector != null && connector.connected();`

Let me write it. Also add `optionalText`.

Note: `json(exchange, 200, Map)` — the projection is a Map<String,Object>. Fine.

Also: should `expectedRevision` be required? If missing → `number(null)` → NPE? `number(Object value)` = `value instanceof Number ? ... : Long.parseLong(String.valueOf(null))` → "null" → NumberFormatException → not caught by guard (it's a RuntimeException but not IllegalArgument/IllegalState/Jackson/Ji) → uncaught → the HttpServer handler throws. Hmm, `guard` catches IllegalArgumentException (NumberFormatException extends IllegalArgumentException) → 400. Good.

