The data directory in LocalHostApplication is `configuredDataDirectory(environment)`. host.db is at `dataDirectory/host.db`. Note `JiCli.composition` already creates SqliteProviderProfileStore on `dataDirectory.resolve("host.db")`. Two connections to the same SQLite file — that's already the case (PersistentHostStore + SqliteProviderProfileStore). Fine (WAL mode, busy_timeout).

So in LocalHostApplication:
```java
java.nio.file.Path dataDirectory = configuredDataDirectory(environment);
var deviceStore = new FileHostDeviceStore(dataDirectory.resolve("host-identity.json"));
var devices = ...;
var relayStore = new SqliteRelaySettingsStore(dataDirectory.resolve("host.db"));
var relayEnrollment = new RelayEnrollment(relayStore, (settings, context) -> new HostRelayConnector(
        settings.managementUrl(), settings.webSocketUrl(), settings.tenantId(), hostId,
